    "title": "Who presents the Green Jacket to Rory McIlroy now that he has won the Masters again?",
    "text": "RORY MCILROY has secured back-to-back Masters victories after a brilliant performance at Augusta. Tradition at the Masters is for the previous year’s champion to present the Green Jacket to the new winner. Sign up for the Sport newsletter Thank you! Scottie Scheffler presented the Green Jacket to Rory McIlroy last yearCredit: Sportsfile The Northern Irishman held a record six-shot lead at the tournament after two roundsCredit: Getty However, McIlroy winning back-to-back titles has led fans to wonder who would present it to him this year, and SunSport has all the details. Who presents the Green Jacket to Rory McIlroy if he wins the Masters again? Last year, Scottie Scheffler was the man to put the iconic Green Jacket on McIlroy since he won it in 2024. This year, the Augusta National chairman Fred Ridley would be the one to do the honours if he is to get over the line. This has only happened three times before, and would put McIlroy in legendary company. To do so, he needs to beat the man he played with on the first two days of action this week – Cameron Young. Tiger Woods was presented the Green Jacket in 2002 by Augusta National Golf Club Chairman Hootie JohnsonCredit: Reuters Comments",
